<title>BAHRAIN: Arab fund lends Bahrain $49.7 mln for housing.</title>
<headline>Arab fund lends Bahrain $49.7 mln for housing.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Arab Fund for Economic Development has given Bahrain an 18.75 million dinar ($49.7 million) loan to finance government housing projects, the official Gulf News Agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>It said Bahrain's Finance and National Economy Minister Ibrahim Abdel-Karim signed the loan with the Kuwait-based fund.</p>
<p>Abdel-Karim said Bahrain was seeking more loans from Arab and Islamic financial institutions to finance development projects. Bahrain plans to spend around 900 million dinars in five years on the projects.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.377 dinars)</p>
</text>
